@startuml state_machines_handover
!theme cyborg
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam backgroundColor #0b1018
skinparam defaultFontColor #e6edf7
skinparam ArrowColor #a9b8ca
skinparam state {
 BackgroundColor #16324a
 BorderColor #4aa3df
 FontColor #e6edf7
 BackgroundColor<<terminal>> #3a1d22
 BorderColor<<terminal>> #e06c75
 BackgroundColor<<finding>> #3a2a12
 BorderColor<<finding>> #e5a50a
 BackgroundColor<<documented>> #273241
 BorderColor<<documented>> #61738a
 FontColor<<documented>> #b8c4d4
}
skinparam note {
 BackgroundColor #1b2330
 BorderColor #61738a
 FontColor #e6edf7
}
hide empty description
title Network/audio handover: when may CONTROL treat the network work as released?\n(implemented; communication.c PendingWork, stopWiFiWork, waitForWiFiStop)
state "Per network service (7 bits in PendingWork)" as Service {
  state "Not running\nbit clear" as Clear
  state "Accepted or running\nbit set before the start call,\nso a partly started service is stopped too" as Running
  state "Stop requested\nwork->stop() with its own bounded wait" as Stopping
  state "Release proven\nstop returned 0; bit cleared" as Released
  state "Release unproven\nbit stays set" as Unproven <<terminal>>
  [*] --> Clear
  Clear --> Running : start call
  Running --> Clear : terminal completion inside the activity\n(L1 has already released its resources)
  Running --> Stopping : Start observed, or the activity's own deadline
  Stopping --> Released : 0
  Stopping --> Unproven : error or timeout
  Released --> Clear
}
state "Acknowledgement to CONTROL" as Acknowledgement {
  state "Running\nState = RUNNING" as NotAcknowledged
  state "Stopped\nState = STOPPED, ListeningIsRequested" as Acknowledged
  [*] --> NotAcknowledged
  NotAcknowledged --> Acknowledged : thread in Listening branch after stopWiFiWork()\n[all bits clear, or cleanup fault latched]
  Acknowledged --> NotAcknowledged : postEvent(Start or Stop):\na new confirmation is needed
}
Unproven --> Acknowledged : latchCleanupFault():\nnetwork disabled until restart;\naudio may start (REQ-13 exception)
note bottom of Service
 Stop order (communication_WorkList): time synchronization, secure connection,
 scan, connect request, setup page, DHCP server, hotspot.
 A retained station association and a retained TLS connection are not work.
 **Unclear:** the design lists five setup services with one total stop bound (P23);
 the implementation tracks seven bits and has no total cap. No total bound is drawn.
end note
note bottom of Acknowledgement
 communication_waitForWiFiStop returns 0 only for ListeningIsRequested and
 State STOPPED or OFFLINE; otherwise it polls in 200 ms steps until its timeout.
end note
@enduml
